Track 1: The Bell-Buoy Bit the Hawser
- Story & Context: In the damp, brine-crusted booth of the Salt-Dock Picture House, projectionist Barnaby Vane first collided brass with dance-punk when his sousaphone bell clipped the spinning drive-belt of a Simplex projector during an illegal screening of a nonexistent silent film about a harbor mutiny. As the machine belched vinegar fumes and locked into an accidental 130-BPM disco gallop, Vane leaned his mouth against the brass and screamed "Thread the blank, crank the tank!" over an avalanche of unhinged cowbell hits and warm tape fuzz. By dawn, forty drenched dockworkers had kicked through the fire door, violently dancing in ankle-deep bilge water to the heaviest pneumatic sub-bass the docks had ever registered.
