Track 2: Whose Shutter Jammed the Tide?
- Story & Context: Holed up in the grease-blackened boiler room beneath the municipal slipways, tape-manipulator Corinne "Gimlet" O’Shea confessed into a dictaphone that she had deliberately dissolved six reels of harbor authority surveillance footage in solvent to create thirty minutes of translucent acetate to project during warehouse lock-ins. Her hands shook from exhaustion as she recorded herself humming sleepy, fireside minor chords through a muffled tuba mouthpiece, suddenly interrupted by a frantic nu-rave synth lead while she chanted "Keep the beacon blind, leave the bass behind!" into an overdriven telephone receiver. The resulting track became an illicit anthem among ferry crews, who used its thumping, wool-padded brass pulse to shake frost off the hull plates.
